From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] esp32p4: initialize active regulator sleep controls

Match pmu_hp_system_init(PMU_MODE_HP_ACTIVE) in ESP-IDF
9a97f6c54ec638111ce55cd36581b3c192f15207 after voltage initialization.
Clear SLP_MEM_XPD, SLP_LOGIC_XPD and SLP_LOGIC_DBIAS in both P4 layouts.
Preserve calibrated DBIAS, DCDC ownership and the SLP_MEM_DBIAS field,
which IDF's initializer does not write.

---
diff --git a/bsps/riscv/esp32/start/bspvoltage.h b/bsps/riscv/esp32/start/bspvoltage.h
--- a/bsps/riscv/esp32/start/bspvoltage.h
+++ b/bsps/riscv/esp32/start/bspvoltage.h
@@ -180,6 +180,10 @@ static void bsp_voltage_init( void )
   }
 #endif
   bsp_voltage_field( 0x28, BSP_BIT32( 18 ), 0 );
+  /* pmu_hp_system_init(ACTIVE): do not retain reset sleep-LDO controls. */
+  bsp_voltage_field( 0x28,
+    BSP_BIT32( 16 ) | BSP_BIT32( 17 ) | ( 15u << 23 ), 0 );
+
   WRITE_REG( VOLTAGE_I2C_BASE, 0x20, select );
 #else
   bsp_voltage_i2c_write( 0x6d, 5, 0x80u, 0x80u );
